<h1>Polling priorities</h1>

<p>A priority sets the band a host's polling interval is kept inside. The maximum
is the guarantee: a host is polled at least that often, however quiet it goes.
The minimum stops a busy host being polled so aggressively that the polling
itself becomes the load. Between the two, the interval adapts to how many events
that host is producing.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Priority</th>
      <th>Rank</th>
      <th>At least every (s)</th>
      <th>Never more often than (s)</th>
      <th>Enabled</th>
      <th>Hosts</th>
      <th></th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @polling_priorities.each do |priority| %>
      <tr>
        <td><%= priority.name %></td>
        <td><%= priority.rank %></td>
        <td><%= priority.max_interval_secs %></td>
        <td><%= priority.min_interval_secs %></td>
        <td><%= priority.enabled? %></td>
        <td><%= priority.windows_targets.count %></td>
        <td><%= link_to 'Edit', edit_polling_priority_path(priority) %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<br>

<%= link_to 'Windows targets', windows_targets_path %>
